WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.705
Preserve original thermal files because they may contain radiometric values, metadata,

00:00:04.705 --> 00:00:07.100
calibration context, palette information, location,

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:10.000
and camera settings that exported screenshots lose.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.955
Keep annotated and processed versions separate.

00:00:11.955 --> 00:00:15.956
Use consistent file names tied to mission, target, date, sensor, and sequence.

00:00:15.956 --> 00:00:19.960
Record environmental conditions, distance, angle, operating state, settings,

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.000
and transformations.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.957
Link each report observation to the source file.

00:00:22.957 --> 00:00:27.215
Annotations should identify areas of interest without hiding the surrounding evidence.

00:00:27.215 --> 00:00:29.995
Include scales and explain palette or range choices.

00:00:29.995 --> 00:00:34.310
Do not use dramatic colors to imply severity that the measurements and context do not

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:34.995
support.

00:00:34.995 --> 00:00:39.000
Report observations, comparisons, confidence, limitations, and plausible alternatives.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.510
State whether values are qualitative or radiometric and whether a specialist reviewed

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:43.995
them.

00:00:43.995 --> 00:00:47.220
Recommend proportionate follow-up rather than announcing a failure from one image.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.000
Thermal imagery may expose people, occupancy patterns, property conditions,

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.000
security features, or sensitive operations.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Apply access control, encrypted storage and transfer where appropriate,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.945
purpose-based retention, and restricted distribution.

00:00:59.945 --> 00:01:04.000
Do not use thermal imaging for stalking, harassment, unlawful surveillance,

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.945
targeting private individuals, or intrusive observation without authority.

00:01:06.945 --> 00:01:11.000
Ethical work is necessary, proportionate, transparent to accountable reviewers,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.890
and careful about both collection and interpretation.
